d event (fired only on insufficient-mana refusal, distinct from ManaSpent), satisfying AC-001/AC-002, with no additions to its public surface beyond mana/regen-delay ownership (AC-003) — no changes were needed there. Fixed the validator's blocking finding in PlayerManaUI.cs: normalColor is now captured from the fill Image's actual color in OnEnable (after mana subscription) instead of relying on the hardcoded Color.white field initializer, so the denied-flash revert restores whatever color the scene/artist configured (e.g. the production scene's blue fill) rather than permanently recoloring the indicator to white.\",\"claimed_changed_paths\":[\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerManaUI.cs\"],\"blockers\":[],\"notes\":[\"PlayerMana.cs was already fully implemented (ResetMana, CastDenied) prior to this session's edits and required no changes.\",\"Did not touch the scene file; the fix works purely at runtime by reading fillImage.color in OnEnable, consistent with the task's execution_reason that no scene/builder changes are required.\",\"Did not run Unity, tests, or any build/package tooling; did not touch test or asmdef files.\"]}","structured_output":{"summary":"PlayerMana.cs already implemented ResetMana() (restores CurrentMana to maxMana and clears the post-cast regen-delay timer to an already-elapsed state) and the CastDenied event (fired only on insufficient-mana refusal, distinct from ManaSpent), satisfying AC-001/AC-002, with no additions to its public surface beyond mana/regen-delay ownership (AC-003) — no changes were needed there. Fixed the validator's blocking finding in PlayerManaUI.cs: normalColor is now captured from the fill Image's actual color in OnEnable (after mana subscription) instead of relying on the hardcoded Color.white field initializer, so the denied-flash revert restores whatever color the scene/artist configured (e.g. the production scene's blue fill) rather than permanently recoloring the indicator to white.","claimed_changed